From 4276b1fd5386c552f6e272c6df219f6990d757c6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: terminills <tdeters@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 11 Jul 2026 17:25:21 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 080/638] [AROS] Keep fork zygote behind its real capability

AI_PHASE: Phase 3 - single-process headless shell
AI_STATUS: AROS no longer compiles Chromium's fork-based zygote path merely because it uses POSIX adapters.
ROOT_CAUSE: use_zygote classified every non-Android, non-Apple POSIX target as fork-capable, while AROS has neither Chromium's Linux zygote delegate API nor concurrent fork semantics.
FIX_REASON: Keep the direct process entry used by single-process headless bring-up and reserve zygote enablement for the future OPAL domain-clone fork contract.
SCOPE: Content zygote feature selection only.
VALIDATION: Generated USE_ZYGOTE is 0 and content_main_runner_impl.o compiles under the AROS target.
RISK: Multiprocess AROS launches cannot use Chromium's zygote optimization until OPAL fork emulation is implemented and integrated.
AI_DECISION_CHAIN: ACD-chromium-native-port-roadmap
Continues: ACD-opal-fork-emulation
---
 content/public/common/zygote/features.gni | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/content/public/common/zygote/features.gni b/content/public/common/zygote/features.gni
index 5f8775d578..aaec688492 100644
--- a/content/public/common/zygote/features.gni
+++ b/content/public/common/zygote/features.gni
@@ -2,4 +2,4 @@
 # Use of this source code is governed by a BSD-style license that can be
 # found in the LICENSE file.
 
-use_zygote = is_posix && !is_android && !is_apple
+use_zygote = is_posix && !is_android && !is_apple && !is_aros
